### What is wrong with a shared pool?

```java
// WRONG: one giant shared pool
ExecutorService sharedPool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(60);
sharedPool.submit(() -> callPaymentGateway());  // 1000 calls/s
sharedPool.submit(() -> getUserProfile());       // 500 calls/s
sharedPool.submit(() -> sendSMS());              // 200 calls/s

// Payment gateway goes down: 30s timeout per call
// 60 threads x 30s timeout = ALL threads consumed
// getUserProfile: QUEUED behind payments
// sendSMS: QUEUED behind payments
// EVERYTHING IS DOWN!
```

### How does the bulkhead pattern fix this?

```java
package com.bank.core;

import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

public class BulkheadConfig {
    private static final AtomicInteger counter = new AtomicInteger();

    public static ThreadPoolExecutor paymentPool() {
        return new ThreadPoolExecutor(
            10, 20, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS,
            new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(100),
            r -> new Thread(r, "payment-" + counter.incrementAndGet()),
            new ThreadPoolExecutor.AbortPolicy() // fail fast: 503
        );
    }

    public static ThreadPoolExecutor userPool() {
        return new ThreadPoolExecutor(
            20, 30, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS,
            new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(200),
            r -> new Thread(r, "user-" + counter.incrementAndGet()),
            new ThreadPoolExecutor.CallerRunsPolicy() // back-pressure
        );
    }

    public static ThreadPoolExecutor notifyPool() {
        return new ThreadPoolExecutor(
            5, 10, 60, TimeUnit.SECONDS,
            new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(500),
            r -> new Thread(r, "notify-" + counter.incrementAndGet()),
            new ThreadPoolExecutor.DiscardOldestPolicy() // drop stale
        );
    }
}
```

Now when the payment gateway is down, only the payment pool is exhausted. User requests and notifications continue normally.

### What rejection policies are available?

| Policy | Behavior | Use case |
|---|---|---|
| AbortPolicy | Throws RejectedExecutionException | Critical: fail fast, return 503 |
| CallerRunsPolicy | Caller thread runs the task | Natural back-pressure |
| DiscardPolicy | Silently drops the task | Non-critical, expendable |
| DiscardOldestPolicy | Drops oldest queued task | Non-critical, prefer fresh |

### How do you monitor each pool?

```java
ThreadPoolExecutor pool = paymentPool();
System.out.println("Active: " + pool.getActiveCount());
System.out.println("Queue: " + pool.getQueue().size());
System.out.println("Completed: " + pool.getCompletedTaskCount());
// Alert: if queue > 80% capacity, pool is saturating
```

